  "plain": "Jeffrey Mishlove, a researcher with a doctorate who studies the mind and psychic claims, says that in the 1970s in Berkeley, California, he was friends with Robert Anton Wilson, a writer on strange ideas and consciousness. Mishlove says that Wilson's beautiful 15-year-old daughter was tragically murdered in Berkeley, and he mentions Wilson's book Reality Is What You Can Get Away With and his ties to the psychedelics figure Timothy Leary."
